  "_note": "DUMMY POLYGONS v1 for the stage-autoscroll feature. Nine 200m x 200m squares strung west-to-east along the north shore of Helenesee (all at 52.283 N, safely on land ~200m north of the water). Larger size so approximate GPS-spoof apps (that only let you pan-drag a map, not enter exact lat/lng) still land inside a polygon. Center-to-center spacing is 0.004° longitude (~272m at this latitude) so there's a ~72m visible gap between adjacent stages. Slug order matches data/timetable.json filters.stages, excluding walking-act (roaming performers, no fixed location). Final polygons will be surveyed on-site later. Feature spec: standalone/docs/floor-detection-plan.md.",
